                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_416">Osney, Oxfordshire. Augustinian
                        abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>Magdalen College, lat. 121--132
                        are a complete collection of glossed books of the Bible collected by John
                        Grene 'Coventriensis' in s. xv med. and all, except perhaps 218, were
                        evidently in the possession of one religious house at an earlier date.
                        Traces of the place-name in 124 and 130 suggest Osney and this is confirmed
                        by the letter-marks and numbers.</p><p>The place-name is of four letters,
                        the second s, the first either u or E. Osney seems virtually certain; cf.
                        MS. 124.</p><p>Grene wrote on fol. iv verso. 'sexta pars biblie ...' (cf.
                        MS. 121).</p><p>'E' (fol. iv verso), and '40' (fol. iv verso).</p><p>Grene
                        wrote on fol. iv verso 'Quinta pars biblie . . .' (cf. MS. 121).</p><q type="pressmark">E; 40</q></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Constat M. J. Grene' (fol. iv
                     verso).</provenance>
               </history>
